---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Workflow" description="How I work with AI agents to build software">
  <h1 class="greet reveal">How I work with <em>agents</em>.</h1>
  <p class="lede reveal reveal-delay-1">
    A loop, not a magic incantation. Each step exists because I've felt the cost of skipping it.
  </p>

  <div class="flow-steps">
    <div class="flow-step reveal">
      <div class="num">01</div>
      <div>
        <h3>Frame the change</h3>
        <p>Before any model sees a prompt, I write what I'm trying to do, who it's for, and what "done" looks like. Two or three paragraphs in a scratchpad. If I can't write it down clearly, I'm not ready to ask an agent to do it.</p>
        <div class="tools"><span>Markdown</span><span>scratchpad</span><span>linear</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flow-step reveal">
      <div class="num">02</div>
      <div>
        <h3>Scout the codebase</h3>
        <p>I let Claude Code read first and write later. The first session is always exploratory &mdash; list files, summarize modules, draft a plan with file paths attached. The output of this step is a written plan, not code.</p>
        <div class="tools"><span>Claude Code</span><span>ripgrep</span><span>tree</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flow-step reveal">
      <div class="num">03</div>
      <div>
        <h3>Tighten the scaffold</h3>
        <p>Most agent failures are environment failures. I make sure types, tests, lints and CI run locally before the first edit, so the agent can self-correct against ground truth instead of vibes.</p>
        <div class="tools"><span>pre-commit</span><span>vitest</span><span>mypy</span><span>biome</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flow-step reveal">
      <div class="num">04</div>
      <div>
        <h3>Edit in small, reversible turns</h3>
        <p>One feature, one branch, one commit per coherent change. The agent moves at the speed of the verifier; if I can't roll a turn back in one keystroke I've made it too big.</p>
        <div class="tools"><span>git worktree</span><span>jujutsu</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flow-step reveal">
      <div class="num">05</div>
      <div>
        <h3>Verify, then trust</h3>
        <p>Tests for the happy path. Property-based or fuzz tests for the boundary. A human reading of anything touching auth, money, or destructive state. Trust scales <em>after</em> verification, never before.</p>
        <div class="tools"><span>hypothesis</span><span>fast-check</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flow-step reveal">
      <div class="num">06</div>
      <div>
        <h3>Capture the recipe</h3>
        <p>If a workflow worked once, I write it down as a skill or recipe so the next session starts further along. Over time these compound into <a href="/projects">agent-eng</a>.</p>
        <div class="tools"><span>agent-eng</span><span>Claude skills</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="closing reveal">
    None of this is rocket science. It's just the part most demos skip &mdash; and the part that turns a flashy autocomplete into something you'd actually let near production code.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .greet {
    margin-top: 6vh;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(32px, 3.8vw, 48px);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    line-height: 1.15;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .greet em { font-style: italic; color: var(--ink); }

  .lede {
    margin-top: 18px;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 560px;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }

  .flow-steps { margin-top: 48px; }

  .flow-step {
    margin-top: 48px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 80px 1fr;
    gap: 24px;
    align-items: baseline;
  }

  .flow-step:first-child { margin-top: 0; }

  .num {
    font-family: 'Geist Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--muted);
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }

  .flow-step h3 {
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .flow-step p {
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 560px;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .flow-step a {
    color: var(--ink);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding-bottom: 1px;
    transition: color 0.15s, border-color 0.15s;
  }

  .flow-step a:hover { color: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); }

  .tools {
    margin-top: 12px;
    display: flex;
    gap: 6px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .tools span {
    font-family: 'Geist Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
    padding: 3px 9px;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }

  .closing {
    margin-top: 96px;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 560px;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .flow-step { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 8px; }
  }
</style>
